    "class": 7,
    "subject": "science",
    "chapter_number": 18,
    "chapter_name": "wastewater story",
    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "What is sludge? Explain how it is treated.",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Semi-solids such as faeces that settle down during wastewater treatment are called sludge. This sludge is removed using a scraper and then transferred to a tank where it is decomposed by anaerobic bacteria to produce biogas. This biogas is used as a low-cost fuel for heating, cooking, etc. It is also used to produce electricity.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Therefore, sludge is treated to produce biogas, which can be used as fuel.",
    "answer_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
